<section class="section faq-reference" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq-grid">
    <div><span class="section-kicker">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</span><h2>Dental questions, answered simply.</h2><p>General information is provided for education. Your dentist can advise you based on your individual condition.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary> کیا ہے؟ RCT</summary><p>Root canal treatment is a procedure used to remove infected or inflamed tissue from inside a tooth, clean the canals and seal them to help preserve the tooth.</p></details>
      <details><summary> سے دانت خراب ہوتے ہیں؟ Scaling</summary><p>Professional scaling removes plaque and calculus from tooth surfaces. It does not normally damage healthy enamel when performed appropriately by a dental professional.</p></details>
      <details><summary> کتنے عرصے چلتا ہے؟ Dental implant</summary><p>Implant longevity varies with oral health, bone support, hygiene, habits and maintenance. Regular dental follow-up helps monitor the implant and surrounding tissues.</p></details>
      <details><summary> ہے؟ Whitening safe</summary><p>Professionally supervised whitening is generally considered safe when appropriate for the patient. Temporary sensitivity or gum irritation can occur.</p></details>
      <details><summary> کب نکالنا چاہیے؟ Wisdom tooth</summary><p>Removal may be considered when a wisdom tooth causes repeated infection, pain, damage, decay or other clinically significant problems. Assessment and imaging help determine the need.</p></details>
      <details><summary>  کب شروع کرنا چاہیے؟ Dental check-up</summary><p>Children should have their first dental visit by the first birthday or when the first tooth appears, followed by regular preventive visits as advised.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

